// Per-developer code signing template.
//
// Copy this to `Signing.local.xcconfig` (git-ignored) and set your Team ID:
//   cp ios/Signing.local.xcconfig.example ios/Signing.local.xcconfig
//
// Find your TEAM ID — it is the certificate's OU (Organizational Unit), NOT the
// id in the cert name's parentheses (that one is the cert's own UID/CN id):
//   security find-certificate -p -c "YOUR NAME" | \
//     openssl x509 -noout -subject -nameopt sep_multiline | grep OU=
// Or: Xcode → Settings → Accounts → your team → Manage… shows it.
//
// The Podfile post_install hook appends an optional `#include?` of
// `Signing.local.xcconfig` to the app's Pods base xcconfig, so running
//   bundle exec pod install
// wires it up. Because the include is optional, a clone WITHOUT this file
// (e.g. CI) still builds — it just won't have a signing team set.
//
// NOTE: building to a physical device from the CLI also needs a provisioning
// profile. `npm run ios` does NOT pass -allowProvisioningUpdates, so the first
// device build per profile must be done via Xcode (⌘R) or:
//   xcodebuild -workspace ios/InkCapture.xcworkspace -scheme InkCapture \
//     -configuration Debug -destination 'id=<device-udid>' \
//     -allowProvisioningUpdates build
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOUR_TEAM_ID
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic
